{
  "format": "fl-mod-source-v1",
  "name": "Thistle Wolf (East Grassy Plains)",
  "notes": "A new early-game wolf for East Grassy Plains (map 25). Reserve monster 274 ('Dummy S-2-3', unit 1406, never spawned in the base game) becomes the Thistle Wolf: monster/unit rows copied from the Red Wolf (monster 11, unit 12) so it shares the wolf's motions, actions, AI, effects and sounds. Like the game's own re-skinned monsters it has its own model and texture resources: the reserve's model leaf 51120 gets a copy of the Red Wolf model (46390) whose material points at the reserve's own texture name mon078_0003_001, and the reserve's texture leaf 51121 (that name, same ETC1 128x128 container) gets art/thistle_wolf.png, painted for the Red Wolf UV layout. The Red Wolf's complete battle-parameter file is copied into the reserve's leaf 51131 with tougher key-1 stats. All three leaves belong to the reserve's own named pack 51122, so no Red Wolf resource changes. Loot block for 274 (Animal Hide 30%, Animal Fang 20%, Oak Log 10%) appended after monster 271; the builder adds the loot terminator row. Spawn group 20 in the East plains table (7290-7298): Thistle Wolf 40% / Red Wolf 60%. One new region in the meadow south-west of the plains centre, (-25, 2.05, 52), in the day layer 23053 and the night layer 23055 (normal layers; 23054/23056 are only used during the Paladin 'Trial of 12' event), with one point forced to the Thistle Wolf. No bounty, no monster-book entry (the book tables 6921-6929 are untranslated cut data in the EU release). See docs/testing/eastern-plains-enemy.md.",
